{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "4a8dd931-5d99-4b28-94b0-fa700ff139bd",
    "name": "RAG API",
    "description": "Postman collection for the RAG API (FastAPI, fully async).\n\n## How to use\n1. Set the `base_url` variable if your server isn't on http://localhost:8000.\n2. Run **Auth → Register** (once), then **Auth → Sign In** — the sign-in request automatically saves the returned `access_token` into the `{{token}}` variable.\n3. Every other request inherits `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}` automatically.\n\nNotes: `/signin` takes a JSON body `{username, password}` (username = your email). For **Delete**, set the `doc_id` variable to a document id from **Read**.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "49731182",
    "_collection_link": "https://go.postman.co/collection/49731182-4a8dd931-5d99-4b28-94b0-fa700ff139bd?source=collection_link"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"user1@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"secret123\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/register",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Create a new user. Returns {id, email, created_at}."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Sign In",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (json && json.access_token) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('token', json.access_token);",
                  "    console.log('Saved access_token to the {{token}} variable.');",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "pm.test('Got an access_token', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().access_token).to.be.a('string');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "packages": {},
                "requests": {}
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"user1@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"secret123\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/signin",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "signin"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Log in (username = email). Saves the returned access_token to {{token}} automatically."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Me",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/me",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Return the current authenticated user. Requires a Bearer token."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
